fullspectrum: consolidated Local-Z stack (replaces former 0053-0068)

Lays down the entirety of the FullSpectrum Local-Z dithering machinery
on top of the {0001-0052 + 0069 + 0070} OrcaXR baseline. Replaces the
former 16-patch series (0053..0068) which carried cumulative duplicates
of earlier patches (0011 BBL append_full_config skip, 0020 brim chamfer,
0021 wall continuity, 0022 wipe-tower bounds fix) and consequently failed
to apply on a clean v2.3.2 baseline.

The merge subsumes:
  * 0053  WipeTower2 Local-Z scaffold (plan_local_z_toolchange/reserve,
          WipeTowerInfo new fields/methods, m_local_z_wipe_tower_purge_lines)
  * 0054  WipeTower2 soluble-depth helpers (layer_has_soluble_toolchange,
          cumulative_toolchange_depth_before)
  * 0055  WipeTower2 Local-Z emission (local_z_tool_change,
          get_local_z_reserve_boxes)
  * 0056  Whole-object Local-Z wiring in slice_volumes
  * 0057  WipeTowerIntegration plumbing (m_local_z_tool_changes,
          m_local_z_reserve_boxes, next_layer cursor reset,
          WipeTowerData::local_z_reserve_boxes)
  * 0058  GCode.tool_change local_z_unplanned param
  * 0059  Print.cpp wipe-tower Local-Z reserve hook
  * 0060  collect_local_z_wipe_tower_toolchanges in Print.cpp
  * 0061..0067  GCode.cpp process_layer Local-Z context, pass prep,
                clipping helpers, mixed-masks union, perimeter clipping,
                emit, base-mask exclude
  * 0068  apply_mm_segmentation painted-path wiring (LZ5c), reusing
          0056's full_cfg.has(k)?opt_bool(k):default style instead of
          referencing the never-defined `bool_from_full_config` helper

Net effect: FullSpectrum's per-sublayer color recipe (PeggyPalette parity
T0=913 T1=939 T2=816 T3=2154 against desktop FS) is now reachable from
OrcaXR. Build chain applies clean from a fresh c724a3f5 v2.3.2 baseline.

Retire-if: upstream OrcaSlicer absorbs the FullSpectrum Local-Z work, OR
a future rebase against a newer OrcaSlicer base obsoletes the line
numbers in this patch. At that point regenerate against the new base.

